From 3f10e92379b37c852af4a07bb5eae32828e07613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:55:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build item 3-1's widening, and measure it as a regression

0108 selected a population by measurement: of 16 426 721 boxed writes
into a numeric-tier-refused local, ElementRead carries 6 908 985 at a
cost/saving of 0.04 and the cascade 7 300 576 at 0.03, while CallResult,
NeverOffered and PropertyRead are refuted at the bound. This admits the
first two and none of the others.

An element read is not provably numeric, so the widened names go to item
3-8a's dual representation -- raw double, live flag, JSValue slot -- and
never to the sound tier. The cascade needs no rule: the pass is a fixed
point, so a name kept only because a widened one was kept is kept with
it. One assume flag, one IsNumeric arm, one extra pass.

Measured against the same build with the switch off, counters on, all
fourteen suites: boxing requests 124 693 165 -> 132 273 724, 1.061, and
boxes allocated 66 982 650 -> 69 582 935, 1.039. It is a regression and
not a small one -- Gameboy alone goes 1.123.

The two counters say exactly why, and it is not the read/write ratio
0108 measured. Roots consumed by a refused local move 18 657 804 ->
18 656 936: 868 of the 18.7 M writes the population was selected for are
actually removed. Speculative-read boxes go 0 -> 7 692 133. So the
saving was never collected and only the cost arrived.

The mechanism cannot collect it. The assignment path tests
NumericStorage, which a speculative local does not have, so it still
asks for the right-hand side as a JSValue, the tree still boxes its
root, and AssignToSpeculativeVariable unboxes it again. 3-8a built raw
arms for the tree's LEAF, the element read and the element write, and
none for the tree's ROOT -- which is the one site the whole saving lives
at.

So 0108's 0.04 was a true measurement of the opportunity and not of
whether any available mechanism could take it. The widening stays off by
default and is kept as the arm a store-path change would be tested
against.

2 further cases, one pinning the diagnosis so it cannot be
rediscovered. NumericLocalDefeatTests now pins the widening in its
control arm, because it is a second speculation path into the same
representation and a run with the environment variable set would
otherwise turn every control into a treatment. 8 173 tests across eight
projects with the switch off, and 1 290 with it forced on.
